       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine for adults, which is 10 mg. Usual doses are 2.5\u201310 mg once daily. An overdose can cause profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock that is hard to reverse.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, a lower starting dose, for example for a frail patient\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
